//@version=5
// v1.2 (2026-05-28): pack_get now returns 7 elements (was 6) — adds tp_id at
// position 3, matching what AFZT Core v11.4 unpacks at line 2448 ([_pf,_pp,_pb,
// _ptpid,_pn,_pr,_pd]). The previously-published AFZT_PackRec/9 had been bumped
// to this 7-tuple at some point; the local template file was stale at v1's
// 6-tuple, causing Core v11.4 to fail compile with "tuple counts don't match"
// until this update. pack_meta/stop_name/be_name signatures unchanged.
// v1.1 (2026-05-28): library title renamed AFZT_PackRec → AFZT_PackRec_Lib →
// "ZT_PackRec_Lib" — TV content-fingerprints any republish under the banned AFZT_
// namespace. Dropping the AFZT_ prefix to "ZT_" mirrors KLP's net-new naming.
// Data block still uses the %%DATA_BLOCK%% template tokens to be filled by
// build_recommendation_pack.py before the v2+ publish.
library("ZT_PackRec_Lib", overlay=false)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// AFZT Pack Recommendation Library
// Phase G-TV: TradingView Downlink Publish Pipeline
//
// Delivery model: TV cannot receive live API push. Instead this library is
// regenerated by the export script (build_recommendation_pack.py) and
// republished to TradingView as a new version. Subscribers receive the
// updated recommendations when they save/reload their chart.
//
// Import in Core (NEVER changes regardless of version):
//   import ragstotrading/ZT_PackRec_Lib/1 as PACK
//
// Generated : %%GENERATED_AT%%
// Window    : %%DT_FROM%% → %%DT_TO%%  (lookback=%%LOOKBACK%%d  min_n=%%MIN_N%%)
// Contexts  : %%CONTEXT_COUNT%%
//
// pack_get() returns:
//   [found, policy_id, be_id, tp_id, n, avg_r, updated_date]
//
//   found       : bool   — true when a qualifying recommendation exists
//   policy_id   : int    — 1=RiskStop  2=ZoneStop  3=ATRStop
//   be_id       : int    — 0=NoBE  1=BE@1R  2=BE@2R
//   tp_id       : int    — TP cap policy (0=use all TPs, 1=stop at TP1, 2=stop at TP2, ...)
//   n           : int    — number of trades in the recommendation window
//   avg_r       : float  — weighted average R for this policy+context
//   updated_date: string — ISO date of the most recent rollup included
//
// Context args:
//   root : syminfo.ticker  (e.g. "ES", "NQ")
//   tf   : timeframe.period (e.g. "5", "15", "60")
//   dir  : 1=Long  -1=Short
//   vol  : 0=LowVol  1=NormalVol  2=HighVol
//   ichi : 0=NoAlign  1=Aligned (pvc + cloud bias both match direction)
//
// If not found returns [false, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0.0, ""] — caller uses default policy.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

export pack_get(string root, string tf, int dir, int vol, int ichi) =>
    // ── DATA BLOCK START — regenerated by export script, do not hand-edit ──
    // %%DATA_BLOCK%%
    // No qualifying data yet — publish pipeline will fill this block.
    // Dummy reference keeps all args alive when data block is empty.
    bool  _found = root != "" and tf != "" and dir != 0 and vol >= 0 and ichi >= 0 ? false : false
    int   _pid   = 1
    int   _bid   = 0
    int   _tpid  = 0
    int   _n     = 0
    float _avgr  = 0.0
    string _date = ""
    // ── DATA BLOCK END ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    [_found, _pid, _bid, _tpid, _n, _avgr, _date]

// ─── Metadata (build date, lookback, min_n) ───────────────────────────────────
// Core can display: TV Pack Version: %%DT_TO%% (%%LOOKBACK%%d/%%MIN_N%%n)
export pack_meta() =>
    ["%%DT_TO%%", "%%LOOKBACK%%", "%%MIN_N%%"]

// ─── Display name helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
export stop_name(int pid) =>
    pid == 2 ? "Zone" : pid == 3 ? "ATR" : "Risk"

export be_name(int bid) =>
    bid == 1 ? "BE@1R" : bid == 2 ? "BE@2R" : "NoBE"
